---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { interests, alsoInterested, papers, plates, REPRO } from '../../data/site';
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const work = [
 { href: '/research/slavemaker', title: 'Slavemaker Swarm', when: '2026', kind: 'Agent-based model', img: 'sm_poster.webp', text: 'Polyergus raids on Formica colonies: thousands of agents coordinated only by five pheromone fields, an enslavement pipeline, queen usurpation, and host–parasite coevolution without an explicit fitness function.' },
 { href: '/research/aeass', title: 'AEASS v3', when: 'CENG 482 (2025), revised fall 2026', kind: 'Paper', img: 'ae_poster.webp', text: 'A memetic algorithm that solves the hardest known 9×9 Sudokus: every one of 65,201 verified runs. An audit of a broken earlier version, and an ablation that shows why local search is essential.' },
 { href: '/research/smart-zebra', title: 'Smart Zebra', when: 'B.Sc. thesis, 2025–26', kind: 'With Onur Kansoy, equal contribution', img: '', text: 'Teaching a 3B language model logic-grid reasoning with SFT and GRPO, using a prompt that follows AC-3 constraint propagation. Funded by TÜBİTAK 2209-A.' },
];
const repro = [
 { name: 'BEECLUST aggregation with Kilobots', src: 'Bodi, Thenius, Schmickl, Crailsheim 2009', status: 'Fig. 5 and the aggregation times of Fig. 7 reproduced in ARGoS; the two-swarm experiments are next.', href: 'https://github.com/EmreErturk-3/swarm-reproductions/tree/main/01_beeclust' },
 { name: 'Onset of collective motion', src: 'Vicsek et al. 1995', status: 'Simulation and figures done; critical exponents still to write up.', href: 'https://github.com/EmreErturk-3/swarm-reproductions/tree/main/02_vicsek1995' },
 { name: 'NEAT on XOR', src: 'Stanley & Miikkulainen 2002', status: 'Solved in 100 of 100 runs, with about 35% more evaluations than the paper.', href: 'https://github.com/EmreErturk-3/swarm-reproductions/tree/main/03_neat2002' },
 { name: 'Gray–Scott patterns', src: 'Pearson 1993', status: 'Phase diagram and pattern classes reproduced.', href: 'https://github.com/EmreErturk-3/swarm-reproductions/tree/main/04_pearson1993' },
];
---
<Base title="Research" description="Research of Emre Ertürk in bio-inspired computing: evolutionary computation, artificial life, swarm and agent-based systems.">
<div class="wrap pagehead"><span class="kicker">Research</span><h1>Bio-inspired computing</h1><p class="lead">How evolution, development and local interaction produce adaptive behaviour, and how to build simulations faithful enough to test these ideas before they reach robots.</p></div>

<div class="wrap section" style="padding-top:10px"><hr class="rule"><div class="rgrid">
 <div class="rv"><h2 class="h2">Interests</h2><ul class="ilist">{interests.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}</ul><p class="also">Also: {alsoInterested.toLowerCase()}.</p></div>
 <div class="rv prose"><h2 class="h2">Direction</h2>
  <p>My interest is bio-inspired computing in general, and at present most of my work is evolutionary. EvoMaxx evolves the rules of an artificial chemistry and measures which rule families make life likely. Slavemaker Swarm coordinates thousands of agents only through pheromone fields. AEASS asks what an evolutionary algorithm needs in order to work on a tightly constrained problem.</p>
  <p>I want to take these ideas further, into bio-inspired, swarm and developmental robotics and robot locomotion. The common thread is simulation: I focus on building realistic simulators in which controllers, collectives and growing bodies can be tried and measured before hardware. That is why I reproduce classic papers first, and why I am learning computer graphics.</p>
 </div>
</div></div>

<div class="wrap section" style="padding-top:0"><hr class="rule"><h2 class="h2 rv" style="margin-top:26px">Papers and reports</h2>
 <ol class="pubs">{papers.map((p) => <li class="rv"><span set:html={p.authors} />. <a href={`${b}${p.to}`}><b>{p.title}</b></a>. <span class="v">{p.venue}</span>{p.links.length > 0 && <span class="pl">{p.links.map((l) => <a class="mono" href={l.href}>{l.label}</a>)}</span>}</li>)}</ol>
</div>

<div class="wrap section"><hr class="rule"><h2 class="h2 rv" style="margin-top:26px">Projects</h2>
 <article class="row rv"><a class="rimg" href={`${b}/research/evomaxx/`}><video src={`${b}/media/research/evo_teaser.mp4`} poster={`${b}/media/research/evo_poster.webp`} autoplay muted loop playsinline></video></a>
  <div><span class="kicker">Artificial life · ongoing since spring 2026</span><h3><a href={`${b}/research/evomaxx/`}>EvoMaxx v10</a></h3><p>A long-running research and creative project. An artificial chemistry on the GPU in which the red, green and blue of every pixel are three chemicals, wired by an evolving eight-gene network; its rule space was mapped by controlled experiments on about 18,000 worlds, and the world plays its own music. Before borrowing from the artificial-life literature, each source was reproduced on its own:</p></div></article>
 <div class="plates rv">{plates.map(([n, t, a, dir, anim]) => <a class="plate" href={REPRO + dir}>{anim ? <video src={`${b}/media/research/repro/r${n}.mp4`} poster={`${b}/media/research/repro/r${n}.webp`} autoplay muted loop playsinline></video> : <img src={`${b}/media/research/repro/r${n}.webp`} alt={t} loading="lazy" />}<span class="pn">{n}</span><b>{t}</b><i>{a}</i></a>)}</div>
 <p class="rv platenote"><a href="/evomaxx/reproductions/live/">All twelve run live in the browser</a>, with the code, figures and a write-up of what did and did not reproduce in the <a href="https://github.com/EmreErturk-3/evomaxx/tree/main/reproductions">repository</a>.</p>
 {work.map((w) => <article class="row rv"><a class="rimg" href={`${b}${w.href}/`}>{w.img ? <img src={`${b}/media/research/${w.img}`} alt={w.title} loading="lazy" /> : <img src={`${b}/media/research/zebra_reward.webp`} alt={w.title} loading="lazy" class="light" />}</a><div><span class="kicker">{w.kind} · {w.when}</span><h3><a href={`${b}${w.href}/`}>{w.title}</a></h3><p>{w.text}</p></div></article>)}
</div>

<div class="wrap section" id="reproductions"><hr class="rule"><div class="grid2" style="margin-top:28px">
 <div class="rv"><span class="kicker">Ongoing</span><h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:8px">Reproductions in evolutionary computation and swarm robotics</h2><div class="prose"><p>Not projects in their own right but continuing groundwork: classic papers re-implemented from the text alone, with the published experiments run again and the mismatches reported. These are the baselines my simulators have to agree with.</p></div>
  <ul class="rlist">{repro.map((r) => <li><a href={r.href}><b>{r.name}</b></a><span class="kicker">{r.src}</span><p>{r.status}</p></li>)}</ul>
  <p style="margin-top:12px"><a class="mono" style="font-size:14px" href="https://github.com/EmreErturk-3/swarm-reproductions">Code and results on GitHub</a></p></div>
 <div class="rv"><figure class="fig"><video src={`${b}/media/research/vicsek.mp4`} poster={`${b}/media/research/vicsek_poster.webp`} autoplay muted loop playsinline style="background:#fff"></video><figcaption>Vicsek reproduction: 1,000 self-propelled particles aligning with their neighbours under noise.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure class="fig" style="margin-top:18px"><img src={`${b}/media/research/beeclust_fig5.webp`} alt="BEECLUST reproduction: fraction of robots aggregated against swarm size" loading="lazy"><figcaption>BEECLUST reproduction, the counterpart of Fig. 5 in Bodi et al. (2009): fraction of Kilobots aggregated in the light against swarm size.</figcaption></figure></div>
</div></div>
</Base>
<style is:global>
.rgrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.8fr) minmax(0,1.2fr);gap:44px;margin-top:28px}.ilist{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;font-size:19px}.ilist li{padding-block:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.also{font-size:15px;color:var(--mut);margin-top:12px}
.pubs{margin:0;padding-left:22px;display:grid;gap:16px;max-width:90ch}.pubs li{line-height:1.5}.pubs a{text-decoration:none}.pubs a:hover b{text-decoration:underline}.pubs .v{color:var(--mut);font-style:italic;font-family:var(--serif);font-size:17px}.pubs .pl{display:inline-flex;gap:10px;margin-left:10px;font-size:13px}
.row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.9fr) minmax(0,1.1fr);gap:34px;padding-block:28px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);align-items:center}
.rimg{display:block;aspect-ratio:16/10;overflow:hidden;border:2px solid var(--wall);background:#0d0d0f}.rimg img,.rimg video{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;transition:transform .5s ease}.rimg:hover img,.rimg:hover video{transform:scale(1.03)}.rimg img.light{object-fit:contain;background:#fff;padding:10px}
.row h3{font-size:clamp(26px,3vw,34px);margin:6px 0 8px}.row h3 a{text-decoration:none}.row p{max-width:60ch}
.plates{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px;padding-top:22px}
.plate{text-decoration:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;position:relative;min-width:0}.plate img,.plate video{width:100%;aspect-ratio:1;object-fit:cover;border:1px solid var(--wall);background:#fff}
.plate .pn{position:absolute;top:6px;left:6px;font:500 11px var(--mono);background:var(--bg);padding:1px 5px;border:1px solid var(--wall)}
.plate b{font-weight:500;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.25;margin-top:7px}.plate i{font:12px var(--mono);font-style:normal;color:var(--mut);margin-top:2px}
.plate:hover b{text-decoration:underline}
.platenote{font-size:15px;color:var(--mut);margin:14px 0 6px}
.rlist{list-style:none;margin:18px 0 0;padding:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.rlist li{padding-block:12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.rlist a{text-decoration:none}.rlist .kicker{display:block}.rlist p{font-size:15.5px;margin-top:4px}
@media(max-width:980px){.plates{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr))}}
@media(max-width:860px){.rgrid,.row{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);gap:18px}.plates{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}}
</style>
